      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have many silly props that I would love to be able to set seat stations on for myself. I could see many creators getting, well; creative with this as well. I think there are too many limitations along with a skill curve when it comes to having to animate your avatar into a pose to work around this. This is a feature I've had pop up in my mind a few times over the years, and it would be great. I'm not sure if the lack of implementation is because we used to have to use world constraints to keep props from traveling with the avatar, and it wouldnt natively work, but we have vrc constraints now, right? it would be great to see an option to enable \"self\" on a seat station, while a prop is constrained in world.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-11-11T17:15:52.988Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "First off, let me explain why. I know, at first glance this seems like a weird request, \"why would you want to sit on yourself\", but the thing is, over time avatar seats have been doing some wild stuff. For example, there's a few teleporters over on Gumroad and Booth, where you can set enter/exit locations. But due to how avatar seats currently work, you can't use them, but others can.\n\nAllowing players to sit in their own seats would open the door to even more unique interactions, toys, gadgets, and more. An example of what could be possible is bringing your *OWN* vehicle to use in racing/driving worlds.",
